name    tttt
prog    /dd/CMDS/tttt
# Tic-tac-toe on a four-by-four board.  It numbers the columns A-D and the
# rows 0-3 and wants them together, `b1'.  It answers a bad square by asking
# again, which is how you can tell it is reading the keyboard at all.
rate    0.6
wait    5
snap    board
keys    b1
key     \r
wait    3
keys    c2
key     \r
wait    3
snap    played
expect  Tic-Tac-Toc-Toe
absent  Can't install trap handler
